# OPC UA floor habits

- Resolve plant NodeIds from a namespace URI plus identifier inside `MiloOpcUaSession.start` on every connect and reconnect. Hardcode `ns=` only for `ns=0` built-in types. Do not add `ns=3` (or any other server index) to YAML, seeds, or tests.
- Trust a value for last-good, interlocks, setpoints, or command ACK only through `QualityGate.requireGood`. Persist Bad/Uncertain telemetry with its `quality` field.
- Build write Variants only in `CommandValueCoercer`, after `OpcUaCommandWriter` has read the target `DataType` attribute. Do not pass a Java double or int where the node is Float or UInt16.
- Reconnect only by closing the session and calling `MiloOpcUaSession.start` again so subscriptions and monitored items are recreated. Do not open a second OPC UA client or reconnect loop.
- Select the endpoint only in `OpcUaClientFactory` from `app.opcua.security.*`. `AnonymousProvider` and `SecurityPolicy.None` are allowed only when that config says so. SignAndEncrypt uses Basic256Sha256 and the configured PKI; missing trust material fails startup. The one exception is the onboarding-probe overload (`createForProbe` / `discoverAndRewriteForProbe`, reached through `OnboardingOpcUaBridge`): it takes the validated request mode as a per-call argument, is Anonymous-only, reads `pki-dir` from `app.opcua.security.pki-dir` and never from the request, and must not mutate the live `OpcUaProperties` the subscription client reads. The live session still follows `app.opcua.security.*`.
- Probe teardown stops at that client's `disconnect()`. Never call `Stack.releaseSharedResources()` and never start or close `MiloOpcUaSession` from the probe — the probe shares the JVM stack with the live subscription client.
- New regressions use `EDGE-NS`, `EDGE-QUALITY`, `EDGE-TYPE`, `EDGE-RECONNECT`, `EDGE-SEC`, or `EDGE-PROBE`. `EDGE-PROBE-M33` is the M3.3 sign-off tag and stays on the single combined Prosys probe call (`i=1001`, `i=1002`, `i=999999`); an `Assumptions` skip of it does not close the milestone.